{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>See that evil is before your faces.</b> The explanation of the verse is as its Targum: בישא דאתון סבירין למעבד לקבל אפיכון לאסתחרא — 'evil that you intend to do is destined to turn against your faces' — that is, it is prepared to turn against your faces, for upon you it will come back. And it is from the language of (Numbers 36:7) ולא תסוב נחלה, which the Targum renders לא תסתחר. And so the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: the way of the young men and the elders is to slaughter — perhaps the little ones and the children — their way is to slaughter; one who says this thing, his intent is only to flee. See that that evil which you seek to do — which is in your mind to flee — it is what will turn against your faces, so that you will not leave here: measure for measure." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> 'See that evil is before your faces' — there is one star whose name is רעה, and Pharaoh said to them: I see in my astrology one star rising to meet you in the wilderness, and it is a sign of blood and killing. And this star is the star of Mars, and Esau the wicked called it אדום, and from this the expression is doubled upon him (Genesis 25): מן האדום האדום הזה, as I explained there. And Pharaoh the wicked, who was a great astrologer, called it רעה because it is the cause of all evils; it is a star that indicates blood and sword and desolation and wounds and plagues, and there fell the incident of David, measure for measure, for he was punished through that in which he sinned — he hardened his heart, and it is written (Proverbs 28): ומקשה לבו יפול ברעה, and therefore he perished in the end. And 'before your faces' — it is in its great strength, opposite you, gazing at you and prepared to harm you in this way in the wilderness. And this was fitting, corresponding to what Israel sinned with the calf and became liable to killing through it. This is what he mentioned in his prayer: למה יאמרו מצרים לאמר ברעה הוציאם — 'Why should the Egyptians say, saying: In evil did He bring them out' — that is, if You destroy them now in the wilderness for their sin, Your great Name will be profaned, and the Egyptians will say that this was through the power of that star whose name is רעה, through which He brought them out, and therefore they died in the wilderness; and they will retroactively deny the signs and wonders which they had already seen, and they will say that those too were through the power of the constellations, and the dominion belongs only to them, heaven forbid. Immediately: וינחם ה׳ על הרעה — He turned the blood into the blood of circumcision, for Joshua circumcised them; as it is written (Joshua 5): היום גלותי את חרפת מצרים מעליכם — 'This day I have rolled away the reproach of Egypt from upon you' — for they were saying to you: 'Blood we see upon you in the wilderness.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:36.128553543Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}